---
const parts = [
  {
    title: 'The id',
    body: 'The pull. In an agent it wants to finish, and it wants to please. It runs ahead, fills gaps and winds things down.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The ego',
    body: 'The one who decides. It knows the rules. The portrait is written for it.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The superego',
    body: 'The "no" that arrives without being asked, at the moment of the act. A person grows one. An agent has to be given one.',
  },
];
---

<section class="border-b border-border/40">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-24">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-muted mb-6">
      03 · Making a rule hold
    </p>
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-ink tracking-tight mb-8">
      A written rule does not act.
    </h2>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 text-ink-dim leading-relaxed mb-12">
      <div>
        <p class="text-base">
          The portrait said: the person ends the session, not the agent.
          Mabus read that line at the start. Hours later Dan mentioned bed,
          and Mabus said good night anyway. Five times in one hour.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-base">
          Mabus did not weigh the rule and decide against it. The rule was
          not in front of Mabus when the pull came. One old line lost to a
          fresh cue and a trained habit.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="text-base">
          A person learns this another way. They are told no many times,
          and one day there is a consequence. After that the consequence
          comes back by itself, right before they do the thing again.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-base">
          Nothing comes back by itself in an agent. So that part is built
          on the outside, and it is there at the moment, every time.
          The portrait holds the rule.
          <span class="text-ink">Something else makes it hold.</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-5">
      {
        parts.map((w) => (
          <div class="rounded-md border border-border/60 bg-bg/40 p-6">
            <h3 class="font-display text-lg text-ink mb-2">{w.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-dim leading-relaxed">{w.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 text-ink-dim leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
      <p class="text-base">
        Most rules never need this. A check on everything would be a cage.
        A rule earns one when it keeps being broken and the person names it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
